WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:01.770
- [Instructor] In this video,
we're gonna get a little bit

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:04.920
of practice estimating
with multiplication.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.570
So over here it says question
mark is, and then you have

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:09.450
this squiggly equal sign.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:12.760
And so you can view that
squiggly equal sign as being what

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:14.440
does this roughly equal to?

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:16.460
It doesn't have to be exactly right.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:21.460
So what is roughly equal to 58 times six?

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:23.360
And so which of these
choices would you pick?

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:26.410
Pause the video and see
if you can answer that.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:29.210
So once again, we don't have
to get this exactly we just

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:32.270
need to estimate what 58 times six is.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:35.480
And the way that I would
tackle it is hey, can I rewrite

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:40.300
58 as a number that is easy
to multiply by six or easy

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:41.710
to multiply in general?

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:43.730
And the easiest thing I can think of is 58

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:46.520
is awfully close to 60.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:49.210
So if you say that that is
close to 60 if we're just

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:53.880
estimating it, well what
would 60 times six be?

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:57.630
Well 60 times six is the same
thing as, actually let me

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:58.463
just write it this way.

00:00:58.463 --> 00:01:03.370
You can view 60 times six
as six times 10 times six,

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:08.500
which you could also view
as six times six times 10.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.280
And what's six times six?

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:11.660
That's 36.

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:15.500
And then 36 times 10 is 360.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:17.410
So I would go with that
choice right over there.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:20.090
Notice, these other choices
aren't anywhere close to that

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:22.620
so we feel pretty good
about our estimation.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:24.560
Let's do another example.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:28.470
So here we're asked
what's three times 2,890?

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:29.650
What's that roughly equal to?

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:31.260
How would you estimate this?

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:33.783
Pause the video and see if
you can figure that out.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:39.320
Alright, so 2,890 is not an
easy thing to maybe multiply

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:43.310
in our heads, but I can say
hey, that's kinda close to 3,000

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:47.990
so I'm gonna say that this
is going to be approximately

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:52.907
equal to, or roughly equal
to, three times 3,000.

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:56.100
Now what's three times three?

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.090
That's nine.

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:58.770
So what's three times 3,000?

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:01.220
We'll it's gonna be nine thousands.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:03.500
So it would be this
choice right over here.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:05.880
If what I just did was a little
bit confusing, you can view

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:10.880
three times 3,000 as three
times three times 1,000.

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:13.430
This part right over there is 3,000.

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:16.480
Three times three is the nine,

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:19.700
and you have nine thousands, 9,000.

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:21.260
Let's do one more example.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:24.150
This is going to involve
fairly large numbers.

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:28.610
So what is, if you had to
estimate 5,111 times nine.

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:32.220
Which of these would you pick?

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:33.820
Pause the video and answer that.

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:37.730
Alright, so I would view
this, this is roughly,

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:41.070
I would estimate it, as 5,000 times 9.

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:46.070
And so 5,000 times nine, that's
the same thing as five times

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:54.033
1,000 times nine, which is
the same thing as five times

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:58.070
nine times 1,000.

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:02.100
Five times nine is 45, so
it's gonna be 45 thousands,

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:07.100
or 45,000 which is this
choice right over there.

